      "id": "source-4",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:30:55Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, accountBalance state before and after the exploit, the deployment transaction, the exploit-time implementation slot, the commit-pinned reproduction, and a complete Upgraded-event query from deployment through the exploit. The exploit calls proxy 0x7c5c9afecf4013c43217fb6a626a4687381f080d, which delegates both forged onERC721Received callbacks to 0xe4764f9cd8ecc9659d3abf35259638b20ac536e4. The malicious collection controls ownerOf and safeTransferFrom, allowing caller-supplied lien data to create an unbacked credit. Two Upgraded events exist; the final event is log 165 of 0x1113e0f43e3f062e91aac24b2901c67bf59d51145078ad668e7de8340d223f24 and selects the recorded implementation. The exploit raises the attack contract's accountBalance from zero to exactly 50.126827091960426151 ETH, the full exchange balance."
    },
